#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Lane D status board (plan §17).

    status --root R --ref REF --ci-results FILE --out DIR
           [--release-tag-glob GLOB] [--push REMOTE] [--include SRC:DEST ...]

Computes every WP's level (L0-L7) and side state, the stage and milestone
state, the decision register, the owner inputs and the §17.3 counters. Every
input is read from REF's tree (`git show REF:path`), never the working tree:
the plan, tests/accept/*, evidence/* and the release tags. GitHub Actions
results come from --ci-results ({"runs": [...]}, see tests/accept/w0c/README).

Writes DIR/docs/plans/STATUS.md and DIR/status/laned_build.json. With
--push REMOTE it commits them (plus any --include files) to branch
laned/build-state on REMOTE, fast-forward only; main is never touched.
Without --release-tag-glob no tag counts as a capability release (no L6).

Levels follow §17.1 (tests/accept/w0c/README) with one addition for a
VERIFICATION WP (accept --help, MODE verification), i.e. one listed in
scripts/laned/verification_wps at REF (any other WP's verification runs are
ignored, RV5): when the ledger has a green `verification` run for the WP, the first first-parent commit at or
after the one adding its PATHS that changes only tests/accept/ files (some
under tests/accept/<wp>/) and whose test dir tree equals the run's `tests_tree` (or whose sha is the run's
`head_sha`) is the merge of that PR and counts as both L1 and L2; the L2
commit is the earlier of it and the implementation commit. L3 and above
follow from it as usual (the push-to-main Accept run on or after it).

L1 comes from a green `expect-fail` run of the WP. A run that records
`tests_tree` (every tests-only PR run) counts only through the commit it
attributes to: the first first-parent commit at or after the one adding the
WP's PATHS that changes only tests/accept/ files, some under tests/accept/<wp>/,
with that tree (`l1_commit`). A batch tests-only squash merge (several WPs'
test dirs, plan rev6.2 (h)) is thereby L1 for each WP via each WP's own
tests_tree, and never an L2 implementation commit for any of them (a
tests-only commit is not one); a verification WP in a batch takes its L2 from
the same commit. Runs without the field (dispatch bootstrap, older entries)
count as before.

L2 is the WP's implementation commit (lanedlib.impl_commit_index). A batch
implementation squash merge (plan rev6.3 (b), accept --help BATCH
IMPLEMENTATION) is the L2 commit of each of its WPs: no tests/accept/ file,
the WP's own PATHS and at most 2 other WPs' PATHS (at REF) match every file
exactly once, each matching some (lanedlib.is_batch_impl_commit).

FEATURE rule (plan rev6.17, accept --help): a PR may carry tests and code for
any number of laned:<WP> labels. LABELLED L2 rule: its squash merge (subject
`... (#N)`) is the L2 commit of a WP iff PR N carried laned:<WP> and the
merge changes a non-test path the WP's PATHS match; a PR whose labels are
known but lack the WP never is (lanedlib.impl_commit_index). Labels: the
`gh pr list` file in $LANED_PR_LABELS plus the ledger's PR rows (field
`pr`). A green `combined` row makes the merge that changes tests/accept/<wp>/
the WP's L1 commit too (`combined_commit`). The git-only rules above apply
only to commits with no PR number or unknown labels.

Ci-only WPs pass L4 automatically (§17.1). L4 for external WPs and an
execution-stage gate need the evidence blob at REF to
have been verified by a green push/accept run (`accept <WP> --evidence F`,
which exports LANED_EVIDENCE=F to the WP's own tests). Invariant coverage
(§17.3) counts only test functions found by AST in
tests/accept/<wp>/**/test_*.py.

    status selftest     # offline check of both rules above
"""

